 111: 
 112: **Locked problems:** 60 twin pairs from 60 unrelated games. Every board is a capture that would lose material if recaptured, and a pinned enemy piece attacks the target square.
 113: 
 114: - 30 **pin pairs:** the only attacker of the target is pinned (good) or the pin line is blocked so it is not pinned (bad).
 115: - 30 **recapture pairs:** the pinned attacker is present on both twins; an extra unpinned attacker is absent (good) or present (bad).
 116: 
 117: **Practice:** 480 trials of idea 1 and 480 trials of idea 2 [choice]. Order is idea 1 then 2 in run 1, idea 2 then 1 in run 2, and alternating blocks of 96 in run 3.
 118: 
 119: **Arms:** Full fly (ideas 1 and 2); idea-1-only fly (480 filler trials in place of idea 2); idea-2-only fly (filler in place of idea 1); fresh fly (960 filler trials); shuffled-feedback fly; plasticity-off fly; simple learner; similar-board recall; exact-recall store; and the **fixed-sum combiner**, which adds the idea-1-only fly's and idea-2-only fly's move scores with a fixed rule. The fixed-sum combiner tests the review's warning that a hand-written rule could combine two answers without the fly learning to combine.
