documentation/current-status.md:3:In the planned test, the researchers looked for settings that made the model rank a safe capture above every other move. They found settings for one of the three positions, short of the two required. After that test failed, a more extensive search found settings for all three positions. That later result is awaiting independent review. The model has yet to demonstrate that it can learn to pick safe captures and apply what it learned to unfamiliar positions.
documentation/current-status.md:9:A three-board feedback test is built and checked, and its run awaits the researcher's approval; nothing has run on the real circuit. It asks whether lessons move the safe capture toward the top more than wrong lessons do, in a quieter version of the circuit. The activity scale for that circuit (0.014047) was checked against a replay of the earlier cell readings: on these boards it caps one cell on two moves in total, across two of the three boards. Codex reports that the full 6,046-connection recheck keeps at least 99% of every move difference. See the [protocol](design/neural-learning/three-board-feedback-test-2026-11-14.md) and the [scale check](../research/reports/fly-connections-memory-v1-2026-11-07/calibration-replay-2026-11-14/README.md). The status below is unchanged.
documentation/current-status.md:15:No full revision-4 learning run is recorded, and the sealed test games remain unused. Properties 1–3 remain unmet; the project has no transferable-reasoning result. See the [November 9 experiment stop report](../research/reports/fly-connections-memory-v1-2026-11-07/stop-report-2026-11-09.md), [checkpoint](next-checkpoint.md), and [dated journal](../research/journal/experiments/2026-11-07-fly-connections-memory.md).
documentation/next-checkpoint.md:9:- **Volume 2, chapters 3 and 5.** A three-board feedback test is built and checked; its run awaits approval. It compares the current circuit with a quiet, rescaled circuit: zero drive, with Kenyon-cell activity read as `min(1, rate / 0.014047)`. It runs correct, swapped-label and learning-off conditions, with fresh memory per board. [Protocol](design/neural-learning/three-board-feedback-test-2026-11-14.md).
documentation/next-checkpoint.md:10:- **Newest run: the calibration replay.** It is complete, made no learner updates, and used no sealed games. Its manifest is dated 2026-11-14 12:04–12:05 UTC, and its local output is `runs/recreated-kc-calibration-2026-11-14` on the replay machine. It regenerated the item-25 cell readings. In the [check](../research/reports/fly-connections-memory-v1-2026-11-07/calibration-replay-2026-11-14/README.md), the scale 0.014047 caps one cell on two moves in total, across two boards (corrected from "one move per board"). The worst move pair keeps 99.0003%. Codex reports rerunning the exact 6,046-connection weighting on the graph machine: at least 99% kept, and all three boards clear the starting-gap cutoff in both circuits.
